1
00:00:01,585 --> 00:00:04,421
I CAN'T BELIEVE
WE'VE NEVER DONE THIS BEFORE.

2
00:00:04,463 --> 00:00:05,923
THIS IS SO GOOD...

3
00:00:05,965 --> 00:00:07,466
SO GOOD FOR MONICA.

4
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:10,761
( bell dings )

5
00:00:10,803 --> 00:00:12,763
OH, LOOK AT THAT.
TIME'S UP. MY TURN.

6
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:16,266
THAT WAS A HALF AN HOUR?

7
00:00:16,308 --> 00:00:17,476
IT'S YOUR TIMER.

8
00:00:19,937 --> 00:00:21,229
ALL RIGHT.

9
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:23,482
YOU KNOW, I
DON'T LIKE TO
BRAG ABOUT IT

10
00:00:23,524 --> 00:00:25,693
BUT I GIVE, LIKE,
THE BEST MASSAGES.

11
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:29,446
ALL RIGHT. THEN
MASSAGE ME UP RIGHT NICE.

12
00:00:29,488 --> 00:00:33,283
AH! AH! AH!

13
00:00:33,325 --> 00:00:35,035
IT'S SO GOOD, ISN'T IT?

14
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:37,496
IT'S SO GOOD, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT I'VE DONE TO DESERVE IT.

15
00:00:37,538 --> 00:00:38,998
OH, GOD.

16
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:41,208
SAY GOOD-BYE TO SORE MUSCLES.

17
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:42,960
GOOD-BYE, MUSCLES.

18
00:00:49,675 --> 00:00:54,930
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

19
00:00:54,972 --> 00:00:57,307
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

20
00:00:57,349 --> 00:01:00,227
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

21
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:04,648
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

22
00:01:04,690 --> 00:01:07,609
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

23
00:01:07,651 --> 00:01:09,653
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

24
00:01:09,695 --> 00:01:13,281
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

25
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:15,367
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

26
00:01:15,409 --> 00:01:17,995
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

27
00:01:18,037 --> 00:01:20,205
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

28
00:01:20,247 --> 00:01:23,417
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

29
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:26,837
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

30
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:36,764
I'M TELLING YOU,
SHE GIVES THE WORST
MASSAGES EVER, OKAY?

31
00:01:36,805 --> 00:01:39,850
IT WAS LIKE SHE
WAS TORTURING ME
FOR INFORMATION

32
00:01:39,892 --> 00:01:41,852
AND I WANTED
TO GIVE IT UP.

33
00:01:41,894 --> 00:01:44,438
I JUST... I DIDN'T
KNOW WHAT IT WAS.

34
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:46,607
LOOK, CHANDLER, IF IT
REALLY HURTS THAT BAD

35
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:48,233
YOU SHOULD JUST TELL HER.

36
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:49,944
LOOK. FOR THE FIRST
TIME IN MY LIFE

37
00:01:49,985 --> 00:01:51,528
I'M IN A REAL
RELATIONSHIP, OKAY?

38
00:01:51,570 --> 00:01:52,988
I'M NOT GOING
TO SCREW THAT UP

39
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:54,615
BY, YOU KNOW,
TELLING THE TRUTH.

40
00:01:54,656 --> 00:01:56,784
HEY.

41
00:01:56,825 --> 00:01:58,285
WHOA, DUDE, LOOK OUT.

42
00:01:58,326 --> 00:02:00,704
DUDE, YOU ALMOST
CRUSHED MY HAT.

43
00:02:00,746 --> 00:02:02,081
I'M-I'M SORRY.

44
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:04,917
AND THE BUNNY
GOT AWAY.

45
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:16,804
THIS WOULD BE THE PLACE
WHERE YOU EXPLAIN THE HAT.

46
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:18,889
OH, YEAH.

47
00:02:18,931 --> 00:02:20,933
THERE'S THIS PLAY, RIGHT?

48
00:02:20,975 --> 00:02:24,144
AND I'M UP FOR THE PART
OF THIS REAL COOL, LIKE,
SUAVE, INTERNATIONAL GUY--

49
00:02:24,185 --> 00:02:25,646
A REAL CLOTHESHORSE.

50
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:27,564
SO I FIGURE EVERYONE
AT THE AUDITION

51
00:02:27,606 --> 00:02:29,942
IS GOING TO BE WEARING
THIS KIND OF, YOU KNOW

52
00:02:29,984 --> 00:02:31,568
ULTRA-HIP,
HIGH FASHION STUFF.

53
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:33,570
AND YOU'RE GOING TO MAKE THEM
ALL DISAPPEAR.

54
00:02:33,612 --> 00:02:35,238
YEAH. LIKE YOU COULD
FIND SOMETHING

55
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,657
AS SOPHISTICATED AS THIS.

56
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:38,033
( derisive chuckle )

57
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:41,870
DONE.

58
00:02:41,912 --> 00:02:43,246
JOEY, IF YOU WANT TO LOOK GOOD

59
00:02:43,288 --> 00:02:45,124
WHY DON'T YOU JUST
COME DOWN TO THE STORE.

60
00:02:45,165 --> 00:02:46,416
I'LL HELP YOU OUT.

61
00:02:46,458 --> 00:02:48,085
OH, GREAT. THANKS, RACH.

62
00:02:48,127 --> 00:02:49,837
SURE.
GOD, PLEASE TAKE THOSE OFF.

63
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:51,170
ALL RIGHT.

64
00:02:52,589 --> 00:02:54,842
Ross:
HEY, PHEEBS,
HOW'S IT GOING?

65
00:02:54,883 --> 00:02:55,843
HEY.

66
00:02:55,884 --> 00:02:57,218
WELL, ONLY OKAY

67
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:59,262
'CAUSE I JUST
GOT BACK FROM
THE HOSPITAL.

68
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:01,389
IS EVERYTHING OKAY?
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

69
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:04,601
I'M FINE. I'M OKAY,
BUT MY GRANDMA SORT OF DIED.

70
00:03:04,643 --> 00:03:06,061
Joey:
OH, PHEEBS, SORRY.

71
00:03:06,103 --> 00:03:08,271
IT'S OKAY.

72
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:10,024
I MEAN, SHE
HAD A REALLY
INCREDIBLE LIFE

73
00:03:10,065 --> 00:03:12,609
AND IT'S NOT LIKE I'M
NEVER GOING TO SEE
HER AGAIN, YOU KNOW.

74
00:03:12,651 --> 00:03:13,819
SHE'S GOING TO VISIT.

75
00:03:16,071 --> 00:03:17,238
WELL, MAYBE...

76
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,573
MAYBE SHE'S
WITH US RIGHT NOW.

77
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:19,783
YEAH, RIGHT.

78
00:03:19,825 --> 00:03:21,743
HER FIRST DAY ON
A NEW SPIRITUAL PLANE

79
00:03:21,785 --> 00:03:24,203
AND SHE'S GOING TO COME
TO THE COFFEEHOUSE.

80
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:25,789
YOU GUYS, YOU GUYS, I JUST SAW

81
00:03:25,831 --> 00:03:27,916
TWO PEOPLE HAVING SEX
IN A CAR RIGHT OUTSIDE.

82
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:33,296
UH, PHEEBS' GRANDMOTHER
JUST DIED.

83
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:34,798
OH. OH, MY GOD.

84
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,091
I'M SO SORRY.

85
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:37,092
IT'S OKAY.

86
00:03:37,134 --> 00:03:38,802
ACTUALLY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

87
00:03:38,844 --> 00:03:41,138
IT'S KIND OF COOL,
'CAUSE IT'S, LIKE...

88
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:43,807
YOU KNOW, ONE LIFE ENDS
AND ANOTHER BEGINS.

89
00:03:43,849 --> 00:03:46,518
NOT THE WAY THEY'RE DOING IT.

90
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:49,479
WHAT... WHAT HAPPENED?

91
00:03:49,521 --> 00:03:51,314
I'M SORRY.
HOW DID SHE DIE?

92
00:03:51,356 --> 00:03:53,358
WELL, OKAY.
WE WERE IN
THE MARKET

93
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:56,236
AND SHE BENT DOWN
TO GET SOME YOGURT

94
00:03:56,277 --> 00:03:59,280
AND SHE JUST NEVER
CAME BACK UP AGAIN.

95
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:00,824
PHEEBS, I'M SO SORRY.

96
00:04:00,866 --> 00:04:01,992
IT WAS REALLY SWEET.

97
00:04:02,034 --> 00:04:03,493
THE LAST THING
SHE SAID TO ME

98
00:04:03,535 --> 00:04:05,537
WAS, "OKAY, DEAR,
YOU GO GET THE EGGS

99
00:04:05,579 --> 00:04:07,497
"AND I'M GOING
TO GET THE YOGURT

100
00:04:07,539 --> 00:04:10,000
AND WE'LL MEET AT
THE CHECKOUT COUNTER."

101
00:04:10,042 --> 00:04:11,210
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?

102
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:13,503
WE WILL MEET AT THE
CHECKOUT COUNTER.

103
00:04:19,843 --> 00:04:21,720
JOEY, YOU KNOW THAT
SINCE YOU'RE RETURNING

104
00:04:21,762 --> 00:04:23,263
ALL THIS STUFF
AFTER THE AUDITION

105
00:04:23,304 --> 00:04:25,849
YOU'RE GOING TO HAVE
TO WEAR UNDERWEAR.

106
00:04:25,891 --> 00:04:29,811
ALL RIGHT. WELL, YOU
BETTER SHOW ME SOME
OF THAT, TOO, THEN.

107
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:32,522
OKAY. IT'S
MISSING SOMETHING.

108
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:34,482
OH, I KNOW.

109
00:04:34,524 --> 00:04:35,859
UM, OKAY.

110
00:04:41,073 --> 00:04:42,407
REALLY? A PURSE?

111
00:04:42,449 --> 00:04:44,118
IT'S NOT A PURSE.

112
00:04:44,159 --> 00:04:46,120
IT'S A SHOULDER BAG.

113
00:04:46,161 --> 00:04:48,705
LOOKS LIKE
A WOMAN'S PURSE.

114
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:50,207
NO, JOEY.
LOOK, TRUST ME.

115
00:04:50,249 --> 00:04:52,042
I'M TELLING YOU,
ALL OF THE MEN

116
00:04:52,084 --> 00:04:54,044
ARE CARRYING THEM
IN THE SPRING CATALOG.

117
00:04:54,086 --> 00:04:56,213
LOOK. SEE? LOOK.
MEN... CARRYING THE BAG.

118
00:04:56,255 --> 00:04:58,048
SEE? LOOK.

119
00:04:58,090 --> 00:05:00,008
WOMEN CARRYING THE BAG.

120
00:05:07,224 --> 00:05:10,144
BUT IT IS ODD
HOW A WOMAN'S PURSE

121
00:05:10,185 --> 00:05:13,021
LOOKS SO GOOD
ON ME, A MAN.

122
00:05:13,063 --> 00:05:14,481
EXACTLY.

123
00:05:14,522 --> 00:05:15,816
UNISEX.

124
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:17,067
MAYBE YOU NEED SEX.

125
00:05:17,109 --> 00:05:18,860
I HAD SEX
A COUPLE DAYS AGO.

126
00:05:20,279 --> 00:05:22,489
NO, NO, JOEY.

127
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,241
"U-N-I" SEX.

128
00:05:24,283 --> 00:05:27,327
WELL, I AIN'T GONNA
SAY "NO" TO THAT.

129
00:05:36,295 --> 00:05:37,587
Ursula:
WHO IS IT?

130
00:05:37,629 --> 00:05:38,922
IT'S PHOEBE.

131
00:05:38,964 --> 00:05:40,299
OH, GREAT.

132
00:05:40,339 --> 00:05:43,260
OH, YOU.

133
00:05:43,302 --> 00:05:44,970
UM, WHAT'S UP?

134
00:05:45,012 --> 00:05:48,765
UM, WELL, I... SORT
OF HAVE SOME BAD NEWS.

135
00:05:48,807 --> 00:05:50,517
CAN I COME IN?

136
00:05:50,558 --> 00:05:53,103
UM, YEAH. NO, THANKS.

137
00:05:54,146 --> 00:05:56,439
UM... WELL... UM...

138
00:05:56,481 --> 00:05:58,775
GRANDMA DIED TODAY.

139
00:05:58,817 --> 00:06:01,111
WOW.

140
00:06:01,153 --> 00:06:04,114
DIDN'T SHE DIE, LIKE,
FIVE YEARS AGO?

141
00:06:04,156 --> 00:06:06,741
NO, SHE JUST DIED TODAY.

142
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:08,660
UM, OKAY.
WE'RE HAVING

143
00:06:08,702 --> 00:06:10,453
A MEMORIAL SERVICE TOMORROW.

144
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:13,372
OKAY. I KNOW I WENT
TO THAT ALREADY.

145
00:06:13,414 --> 00:06:15,125
NO, YOU DIDN'T.

146
00:06:15,167 --> 00:06:16,918
THEN WHO'S BEEN
DEAD FOR FIVE YEARS?

147
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:18,337
WELL, LOTS OF PEOPLE.

148
00:06:18,377 --> 00:06:20,672
LOOK. ARE
YOU COMING

149
00:06:20,714 --> 00:06:22,883
TO THE MEMORIAL
SERVICE OR NOT?

150
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:24,592
UM, NO.

151
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:26,511
SEE, I ALREADY
THOUGHT

152
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:27,721
SHE WAS DEAD

153
00:06:27,762 --> 00:06:29,890
SO I'VE KIND OF MADE
MY PEACE WITH IT.

154
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:33,894
AND PLUS, I'M GOING
TO A CONCERT TOMORROW, SO...

155
00:06:33,935 --> 00:06:35,145
I'D INVITE YOU

156
00:06:35,187 --> 00:06:37,147
BUT I ONLY HAVE
TWO TICKETS LEFT.

157
00:06:38,523 --> 00:06:39,900
FINE.

158
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:41,360
OKAY. ENJOY
YOUR CONCERT.

159
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,028
THANKS. ENJOY
YOUR FUNERAL.

160
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:46,823
HEY.

161
00:06:46,865 --> 00:06:48,200
HEY.

162
00:06:54,622 --> 00:06:57,792
WOW. YOU LOOK JUST LIKE
YOUR SON, MRS. TRIBBIANI.

163
00:06:57,834 --> 00:06:59,586
WHAT?

164
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:02,047
ARE YOU REFERRING
TO MY MAN'S BAG?

165
00:07:03,464 --> 00:07:05,300
AT FIRST I THOUGHT
IT JUST LOOKED GOOD

166
00:07:05,342 --> 00:07:07,219
BUT IT'S PRACTICAL, TOO.
CHECK IT OUT.

167
00:07:07,261 --> 00:07:09,263
IT'S GOT COMPARTMENTS
FOR ALL YOUR STUFF--

168
00:07:09,304 --> 00:07:11,472
YOUR WALLET, YOUR KEYS,
YOUR ADDRESS BOOK...

169
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:12,557
YOUR MAKEUP.

170
00:07:14,601 --> 00:07:15,936
WHAT ARE YOU
DOING WITH THE BAG?

171
00:07:15,977 --> 00:07:17,436
YOUR AUDITION'S
NOT TILL TOMORROW.

172
00:07:17,478 --> 00:07:20,232
YEAH, BUT SANDWICH TIME
IS RIGHT NOW.

173
00:07:20,274 --> 00:07:22,567
JOEY, YOU KNOW YOU GET
ANY MUSTARD ON THAT BAG

174
00:07:22,609 --> 00:07:23,610
YOU CAN'T RETURN IT.

175
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:25,279
WHY WOULD I RETURN THIS?

176
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:26,696
I LOVE THIS BAG.

177
00:07:26,738 --> 00:07:28,782
ALL RIGHT.
THEN YOU OWE ME $350.

178
00:07:28,823 --> 00:07:30,200
Joey:
FINE.

179
00:07:30,242 --> 00:07:33,745
DO YOU TAKE VASA
OR MOOSTERCARD?

180
00:07:33,787 --> 00:07:35,789
JOEY...

181
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:37,457
ALL RIGHT. RELAX.
LOOK. I'LL PAY YOU

182
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:39,126
WITH THE MONEY
FROM THE ACTING JOB

183
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:41,169
I AM DEFINITELY GOING TO GET
THANKS TO YOU.

184
00:07:41,211 --> 00:07:42,837
WHAT'S THE PART? AUNTIE MAME?

185
00:07:44,339 --> 00:07:45,673
DON'T LISTEN TO THEM.

186
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:46,883
I THINK IT'S SEXY.

187
00:07:46,925 --> 00:07:49,469
"YOU AND I" SEXY?

188
00:07:56,268 --> 00:07:57,769
OH, HELLO, MRS. PINELLO.

189
00:07:57,811 --> 00:07:59,562
THANK YOU SO MUCH
FOR COMING.

190
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:01,856
OKAY. HERE'S
YOUR 3-D GLASSES.

191
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:07,195
AND REVEREND PONG WILL TELL YOU
WHEN TO PUT THEM ON.

192
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:12,159
HI, SWEETIE.

193
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,452
HOW ARE YOU
HOLDING UP?

194
00:08:13,493 --> 00:08:14,661
FINE.

195
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:16,330
HEY, PHEEBS.

196
00:08:16,371 --> 00:08:18,165
I'M SO SORRY.

197
00:08:18,206 --> 00:08:19,749
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

198
00:08:19,791 --> 00:08:22,461
MY GRANDMA HAD
THE EXACT SAME BAG.

199
00:08:22,501 --> 00:08:24,587
HERE. I BROUGHT YOU
SOME FLOWERS.

200
00:08:24,629 --> 00:08:26,340
OH, THANKS.

201
00:08:26,381 --> 00:08:27,674
YEAH. PULLING FLOWERS
OUT OF IT

202
00:08:27,715 --> 00:08:29,508
MAKES THE BAG LOOK
A LOT MORE MASCULINE.

203
00:08:30,844 --> 00:08:32,346
OH, I'M SORRY.

204
00:08:32,387 --> 00:08:34,806
EXCUSE ME. IS THIS
THE MEMORIAL?

205
00:08:34,848 --> 00:08:36,141
YEAH. WELCOME.

206
00:08:36,183 --> 00:08:37,142
HELLO.

207
00:08:37,184 --> 00:08:38,477
HERE'S YOUR
3-D GLASSES.

208
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:40,479
OH... ALL RIGHT.

209
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:44,358
SO, HOW DID YOU KNOW FRANCES?

210
00:08:44,399 --> 00:08:45,608
WELL, ACTUALLY...

211
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:48,445
I HADN'T SEEN HER
FOR YEARS, BUT, UM...

212
00:08:48,487 --> 00:08:52,199
WELL, I WAS PRETTY TIGHT
WITH HER AND HER DAUGHTER.

213
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,574
REALLY? WHAT'S YOUR NAME?

214
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:54,742
FRANK BUFFAY.

215
00:08:57,412 --> 00:08:59,539
YOU KNOW WHAT? STRIKE THAT.

216
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:01,916
MY NAME... ACTUALLY, IS-IS JOE.

217
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:03,210
UM...

218
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:04,878
JOE... UH, HILL.

219
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:06,004
YOU'RE FRANK BUFFAY?

220
00:09:06,046 --> 00:09:07,339
( whispering ):
SHH! NO!

221
00:09:07,381 --> 00:09:08,548
JOE HILL!

222
00:09:08,589 --> 00:09:10,925
BUT YOU JUST SAID...

223
00:09:10,967 --> 00:09:12,260
YOU KNOW WHAT? I GOT TO GO

224
00:09:12,302 --> 00:09:13,970
AND THANK YOU
SO MUCH FOR COMING.

225
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:17,098
BUT...

226
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:18,266
OH, MY GOD.

227
00:09:18,308 --> 00:09:19,434
WHAT?

228
00:09:19,476 --> 00:09:20,685
Monica:
WHAT, HONEY?

229
00:09:20,727 --> 00:09:22,270
THAT WAS MY DAD.

230
00:09:22,312 --> 00:09:23,897
OH, MY GOD.

231
00:09:23,938 --> 00:09:26,316
HEY, YOU GUYS, CHECK
IT OUT, CHECK IT OUT.

232
00:09:26,358 --> 00:09:28,360
IT'S LIKE IT'S
COMING RIGHT AT ME.

233
00:09:35,450 --> 00:09:36,410
DID YOU
CATCH HIM?

234
00:09:36,451 --> 00:09:37,411
UH-HUH.

235
00:09:37,452 --> 00:09:38,578
WHAT DID
HE SAY?

236
00:09:38,619 --> 00:09:41,415
HE SAID, "NICE TO
MEET YOU, GLENDA."

237
00:09:41,456 --> 00:09:44,792
WELL, OBVIOUSLY, I COULDN'T
GIVE HIM MY REAL NAME.

238
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:46,127
WHY? WHY NOT?

239
00:09:46,169 --> 00:09:47,754
YOU SAW THE WAY
HE RAN OUT OF HERE.

240
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:49,130
YOU THINK HE'D STICK AROUND

241
00:09:49,172 --> 00:09:50,798
AND TALK TO THE DAUGHTER
HE ABANDONED?

242
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,800
WHAT DID YOU
SAY TO HIM?

243
00:09:52,842 --> 00:09:55,929
I TOLD HIM I WAS THE EXECUTOR
PERSON OF FRANCES'S WILL

244
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:57,972
AND THAT I NEEDED
TO TALK TO HIM

245
00:09:58,014 --> 00:10:01,142
SO I'M GOING TO MEET HIM
AT THE COFFEEHOUSE LATER.

246
00:10:01,184 --> 00:10:02,561
( funeral music playing )

247
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:03,853
ALL RIGHT.

248
00:10:03,895 --> 00:10:05,939
WELL, I JUST CAN'T
THINK ABOUT THAT NOW.

249
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,316
I-I JUST WANT
TO SAY GOOD-BYE
TO MY GRANDMA.

250
00:10:08,358 --> 00:10:09,943
OKAY. LET'S GO
SAY GOOD-BYE.

251
00:10:21,829 --> 00:10:22,789
HEY.

252
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:25,208
I'M OFF
TO MY AUDITION.

253
00:10:25,250 --> 00:10:26,834
HOW DO I LOOK?

254
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:28,211
I THINK YOU LOOK GREAT.

255
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:30,088
JOEY, THAT BAG IS GOING
TO GET YOU THAT PART.

256
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:31,465
AND A DATE
WITH A MAN.

257
00:10:33,091 --> 00:10:34,050
YOU KNOW WHAT?

258
00:10:34,092 --> 00:10:35,594
MAKE FUN ALL YOU WANT.

259
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:37,471
THIS IS A GREAT BAG, OKAY?

260
00:10:37,512 --> 00:10:39,973
AND IT'S AS HANDY
AS IT IS BECOMING.

261
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:42,934
NOW, JUST BECAUSE
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND SOMETHING

262
00:10:42,976 --> 00:10:45,228
DOESN'T MAKE IT WRONG,
ALL RIGHT?

263
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:47,730
SO, FROM NOW ON,
YOU GUYS ARE GOING

264
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:50,775
TO HAVE TO GET USED TO THE FACT
THAT JOEY COMES WITH A BAG.

265
00:10:52,444 --> 00:10:54,613
I BETTER GO, TOO. I
GOT TO GO MEET MY DAD.

266
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:56,615
PHEEBS, ARE YOU
GOING TO TELL
HIM WHO YOU ARE?

267
00:10:56,656 --> 00:10:59,700
NO, NOT AT FIRST,
'CAUSE I DON'T WANT
TO FREAK HIM OUT.

268
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:01,578
BUT AREN'T YOU PISSED
AT HIM?

269
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:03,580
I MEAN, THIS GUY ABANDONED YOU.

270
00:11:03,622 --> 00:11:05,582
I GOT TO TELL YOU,
IF IT WERE ME

271
00:11:05,624 --> 00:11:08,251
THIS GUY WOULD BE
IN SOME SERIOUS PHYSICAL DANGER.

272
00:11:08,293 --> 00:11:10,753
I-I-I'D WALK IN THERE...

273
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:17,218
I'D BE, LIKE, "YO, DAD!
YOU AND ME OUTSIDE RIGHT NOW!"

274
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:19,471
I KIND OF SCARED MYSELF.

275
00:11:19,513 --> 00:11:24,392
WELL, AT LEAST YOU
SCARED SOMEONE.

276
00:11:24,434 --> 00:11:25,768
YOU KNOW, IT'S FUNNY.

277
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:27,562
YOU'D THINK I'D BE ANGRY.

278
00:11:27,604 --> 00:11:30,649
I MEAN, YOU'D THINK
I'D WANT TO RIP HIS
TINY LITTLE HEAD OFF.

279
00:11:30,689 --> 00:11:34,027
FORTUNATELY, I'M PAST IT, SO...

280
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:36,237
PHOEBE, YOU DO SEEM
A LITTLE TENSE.

281
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:37,531
HERE. LET ME HELP YOU.

282
00:11:37,572 --> 00:11:38,573
ALL RIGHT.

283
00:11:38,615 --> 00:11:39,574
GET OFF!

284
00:11:39,616 --> 00:11:41,618
OW! OH, STOP IT!

285
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:43,744
WHY? WHY ARE YOU
DOING THAT TO ME?!

286
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:45,746
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

287
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:48,249
AS A MASSEUSE AND A HUMAN

288
00:11:48,291 --> 00:11:52,462
I'M BEGGING YOU,
NEVER DO THAT TO ANYONE.

289
00:11:52,504 --> 00:11:55,131
I GIVE GOOD MASSAGES.

290
00:11:55,173 --> 00:11:56,508
( scoffs )

291
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:58,968
I USED TO GIVE THEM
TO RACHEL ALL THE TIME

292
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:00,512
BEFORE SHE GOT ALLERGIC.

293
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:03,890
AND CHANDLER...

294
00:12:03,931 --> 00:12:05,308
HE LOVES THEM. WATCH.

295
00:12:07,519 --> 00:12:08,645
HE DOES NOT LIKE IT.

296
00:12:08,687 --> 00:12:10,063
HE HATES IT.
HE'S IN PAIN.

297
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:11,314
NO, HE'S NOT.

298
00:12:11,356 --> 00:12:12,815
YES, HE IS.

299
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:14,025
WHAT?

300
00:12:14,067 --> 00:12:16,611
I'M SORRY, BUT... OW! OW! OW!

301
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:22,825
HAVE YOU BEEN
LYING TO ME?

302
00:12:22,867 --> 00:12:24,785
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU'D DO THAT.

303
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:27,038
MAYBE HE JUST DIDN'T WANT
TO HURT YOUR FEELINGS.

304
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:29,999
BUT THE MINUTE WE START
TO LIE TO EACH OTHER...

305
00:12:33,545 --> 00:12:34,921
AND BY "WE"

306
00:12:34,962 --> 00:12:37,257
I MEAN SOCIETY...

307
00:12:39,634 --> 00:12:42,429
ANY TIME YOU'RE
READY, JOEY.

308
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,138
"WELL, YOU MUST BE NEW HERE.

309
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:46,349
MAYBE WE GET A TABLE
AND I BUY YOU A DRINK."

310
00:12:46,391 --> 00:12:47,766
I'M SORRY.

311
00:12:47,808 --> 00:12:50,228
COULD YOU... COULD YOU TRY IT
WITHOUT THE PURSE?

312
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:53,231
YEAH. SURE.

313
00:12:57,235 --> 00:12:59,862
"WELL, YOU MUST
BE NEW HERE.

314
00:12:59,904 --> 00:13:01,489
"MAYBE WE SIT...

315
00:13:01,531 --> 00:13:03,533
I'M SORRY.
CAN I ASK YOU SOMETHING?

316
00:13:03,575 --> 00:13:04,743
SURE. WHAT?

317
00:13:04,783 --> 00:13:07,579
WELL, FIRST, IT'S NOT A PURSE.

318
00:13:07,621 --> 00:13:10,624
OKAY. ANY TIME.

319
00:13:10,665 --> 00:13:13,418
I MEAN, IF YOU'RE THINKING
IT'S A WOMAN'S BAG, IT'S NOT.

320
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:15,503
IT'S A MAN'S BAG.

321
00:13:15,545 --> 00:13:19,466
OKAY, AND GO.

322
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:22,636
LET ME SHOW
YOU THE CATALOG.

323
00:13:22,677 --> 00:13:24,429
LOOK. SEE? HUH?

324
00:13:24,471 --> 00:13:26,180
IT'S THE
LATEST THING.

325
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:27,724
EVERYONE'S
GOT ONE:

326
00:13:27,766 --> 00:13:28,891
MEN, WOMEN,
CHILDREN.

327
00:13:28,933 --> 00:13:30,310
EVERYONE'S
CARRYING THEM.

328
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:32,061
DO YOU SELL THESE BAGS?

329
00:13:32,103 --> 00:13:35,273
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.

330
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:38,025
THESE BABIES SELL THEMSELVES.

331
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:39,152
OKAY. THANK YOU.

332
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:40,528
THAT WAS GREAT.

333
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:42,447
YEAH, BUT I DIDN'T EVEN READ
ANYTHING.

334
00:13:42,489 --> 00:13:44,823
I THINK WE'VE SEEN ENOUGH.

335
00:13:44,865 --> 00:13:48,161
OKAY. ALL RIGHT. I'LL SEE YOU.

336
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:50,705
WE GOT IT, WE GOT IT.

337
00:13:51,914 --> 00:13:53,750
HEY, IS RACHEL HERE?

338
00:13:53,792 --> 00:13:55,084
NO.

339
00:13:55,126 --> 00:13:57,295
LISTEN, I JUST WANTED
TO APOLOGIZE

340
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:58,630
ABOUT THIS AFTERNOON

341
00:13:58,672 --> 00:14:01,090
AND THE WHOLE MASSAGE
THING, YOU KNOW?

342
00:14:01,132 --> 00:14:02,883
I-I REALLY LIKE THEM.

343
00:14:02,925 --> 00:14:05,428
PLEASE, STOP.

344
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:07,138
WE'RE SUPPOSED
TO BE HONEST

345
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:08,181
WITH EACH OTHER.

346
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:10,141
I JUST WISH
YOU COULD TELL ME.

347
00:14:10,183 --> 00:14:12,811
JUST SAY IT:
"I DON'T LIKE
YOUR MASSAGES."

348
00:14:16,731 --> 00:14:21,110
I DON'T LIKE
YOUR MASSAGES.

349
00:14:21,152 --> 00:14:24,572
( voice breaking ):
SEE? IT'S NO BIG DEAL.

350
00:14:24,614 --> 00:14:25,699
OKAY, BUT NOW, SEE?

351
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:26,783
YOU'RE CRYING.

352
00:14:26,825 --> 00:14:28,284
I'M NOT CRYING
ABOUT THAT.

353
00:14:28,326 --> 00:14:29,786
I'M CRYING
ABOUT SOMETHING

354
00:14:29,828 --> 00:14:31,120
THAT HAPPENED AT WORK.

355
00:14:31,162 --> 00:14:32,455
WHAT?

356
00:14:32,497 --> 00:14:34,791
MY BOYFRIEND SAID HE
DIDN'T LIKE MY MASSAGES!

357
00:14:34,833 --> 00:14:36,835
IT'S OKAY.

358
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:39,504
YOU DON'T HAVE TO BE
THE BEST AT EVERYTHING.

359
00:14:39,546 --> 00:14:41,381
OH, MY GOD!

360
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:44,133
YOU DON'T KNOW ME AT ALL!

361
00:14:44,175 --> 00:14:49,180
OKAY. YOU GIVE THE WORST
MASSAGES IN THE WORLD.

362
00:14:49,222 --> 00:14:51,474
I'M CRYING HERE!

363
00:14:51,516 --> 00:14:52,517
WELL, ALL RIGHT.

364
00:14:52,559 --> 00:14:53,768
HEAR ME OUT, OKAY?

365
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:56,187
YOU GIVE THE BEST
BAD MASSAGES, OKAY?

366
00:14:56,229 --> 00:14:59,315
IF ANYBODY WAS LOOKING
FOR THE BEST BAD MASSAGE

367
00:14:59,357 --> 00:15:01,651
AND THEY WERE THINKING
TO THEMSELVES

368
00:15:01,693 --> 00:15:03,361
"WHO'S THE BEST AT THAT?"

369
00:15:03,403 --> 00:15:05,112
THEY'D HAVE TO GO TO YOU.

370
00:15:08,115 --> 00:15:11,077
HUH.

371
00:15:11,118 --> 00:15:13,663
SO, YOU'RE SAYING
THAT, LIKE, UM...

372
00:15:13,705 --> 00:15:17,250
IF THERE WAS AN AWARD
FOR THE BEST BAD MASSAGE...

373
00:15:17,291 --> 00:15:19,293
WELL, WHO WOULD GET THAT?

374
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:20,712
OH, IT WOULD BE YOU.

375
00:15:20,754 --> 00:15:21,880
YOU, MONICA

376
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,549
AND YOU'D GET
ALL THE VOTES.

377
00:15:24,591 --> 00:15:28,135
SO, MAYBE THEY COULD, UM,
CALL THE AWARD "THE MONICA"?

378
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:31,514
ABSOLUTELY.

379
00:15:31,556 --> 00:15:34,350
OKAY.

380
00:15:34,392 --> 00:15:35,393
I SUCK.

381
00:15:35,435 --> 00:15:36,477
YEAH.

382
00:15:42,734 --> 00:15:44,903
THANK YOU FOR MEETING WITH ME.

383
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:46,529
THANK YOU. ALL RIGHT.

384
00:15:46,571 --> 00:15:50,199
COME SIT.

385
00:15:50,241 --> 00:15:52,619
SIT.

386
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:55,329
SIT!

387
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:56,539
UM, ALL RIGHTY.

388
00:15:56,581 --> 00:15:58,917
UM, BEFORE WE GET
STARTED, I'D JUST...

389
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,126
I NEED YOU TO STATE

390
00:16:00,167 --> 00:16:01,586
FOR THE, YOU KNOW,
OFFICIAL RECORD

391
00:16:01,628 --> 00:16:03,337
THAT YOU ARE, IN FACT,
FRANK BUFFAY.

392
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:05,548
OH, YES. YES, YES, I AM. MM-HMM.

393
00:16:05,590 --> 00:16:06,883
OKAY.

394
00:16:06,925 --> 00:16:08,217
SO...

395
00:16:08,259 --> 00:16:10,219
WHAT DID FRANCES LEAVE ME?

396
00:16:10,261 --> 00:16:11,638
HUH?

397
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:13,222
THAT'S WHY YOU WANTED
ME TO COME, RIGHT?

398
00:16:13,264 --> 00:16:14,808
OH, YES.

399
00:16:14,849 --> 00:16:16,976
YES. YEAH. NO, SHE DID.

400
00:16:17,017 --> 00:16:18,812
SHE LEFT YOU, UM...

401
00:16:18,853 --> 00:16:21,230
THIS LIPSTICK.

402
00:16:21,272 --> 00:16:24,150
OH... HUH.

403
00:16:24,191 --> 00:16:26,068
THAT'S...

404
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:29,447
OH, IT'S USED.

405
00:16:29,489 --> 00:16:33,075
UH, COOL.

406
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:36,496
OKAY. I HAVE JUST
A FEW QUESTIONS TO ASK

407
00:16:36,537 --> 00:16:39,874
SO I'M GOING TO GET
OUT MY OFFICIAL FORMS.

408
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:45,254
OKAY. SO, QUESTION ONE:

409
00:16:45,296 --> 00:16:48,341
YOU WERE MARRIED
TO FRANCES'S DAUGHTER, LILY.

410
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:49,843
IS THAT CORRECT?

411
00:16:49,884 --> 00:16:52,052
YES. YES, I WAS.

412
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:54,347
OKAY. UM, QUESTION TWO:

413
00:16:54,388 --> 00:16:59,435
UM, "DID THAT MARRIAGE END,
A: HAPPILY, B: MEDIUM

414
00:16:59,477 --> 00:17:05,733
OR C: IN THE TOTAL ABANDONMENT
OF HER AND HER TWO CHILDREN?"

415
00:17:05,775 --> 00:17:07,777
IT REALLY SAYS THAT?

416
00:17:07,819 --> 00:17:10,279
YEAH. SEE?

417
00:17:10,321 --> 00:17:13,533
WELL, I GUESS
THAT I WOULD
HAVE TO SAY "C."

418
00:17:13,574 --> 00:17:14,617
HMM. OKAY.

419
00:17:14,659 --> 00:17:16,786
TOTAL ABANDONMENT, MM-HMM.

420
00:17:16,828 --> 00:17:20,080
OKAY. "REASONS
FOR ABANDONMENT."

421
00:17:20,122 --> 00:17:25,586
UM, "A: TOP SECRET
GOVERNMENT WORK, B: AMNESIA

422
00:17:25,628 --> 00:17:31,592
OR C: YOU'RE JUST A SELFISH,
IRRESPONSIBLE, BAD, BAD MAN?"

423
00:17:31,634 --> 00:17:34,595
YOU KNOW, I DON'T
THINK I WANT THE
LIPSTICK THAT MUCH

424
00:17:34,637 --> 00:17:37,807
BUT, UH... OH, WOULD
YOU DO ME A FAVOR

425
00:17:37,849 --> 00:17:41,602
AND, UM, WOULD YOU GIVE
HER DAUGHTER LILY

426
00:17:41,644 --> 00:17:43,730
THAT, PLEASE?

427
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:44,731
WHAT?

428
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:45,815
LILY. WHEN YOU
SEE LILY

429
00:17:45,857 --> 00:17:47,274
WOULD YOU GIVE
HER THAT NOTE

430
00:17:47,316 --> 00:17:49,819
BECAUSE I WANTED
TO TALK TO HER
AT THE MEMORIAL.

431
00:17:49,861 --> 00:17:53,447
WELL, I PICTURED HER GETTING MAD
AT ME THE WAY YOU GOT MAD AT ME

432
00:17:53,489 --> 00:17:56,075
AND I CHICKENED OUT,
SO I WROTE HER THAT NOTE.

433
00:17:56,116 --> 00:17:57,994
WOULD YOU GIVE IT TO HER,
PLEASE?

434
00:17:58,036 --> 00:18:00,830
YOU-YOU-YOU CAME TO SEE LILY?

435
00:18:00,872 --> 00:18:02,957
YEAH, YEAH. WHY?

436
00:18:02,999 --> 00:18:05,084
LILY'S DEAD.

437
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:08,504
SHE WHAT?

438
00:18:08,546 --> 00:18:10,339
SHE'S DEAD.

439
00:18:10,381 --> 00:18:11,591
ARE YOU SURE?

440
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:12,842
WELL, IF SHE ISN'T

441
00:18:12,884 --> 00:18:14,969
CREMATING HER WAS BIG MISTAKE.

442
00:18:15,011 --> 00:18:17,680
I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS.

443
00:18:17,722 --> 00:18:19,515
I JUST CAN'T BELIEVE IT.

444
00:18:19,557 --> 00:18:22,142
HOW, HOW...? OH, MY GOD.

445
00:18:22,184 --> 00:18:24,144
HOW-HOW LONG AGO?

446
00:18:24,186 --> 00:18:25,813
17 YEARS AGO.

447
00:18:25,855 --> 00:18:27,523
OH...

448
00:18:27,565 --> 00:18:30,651
WHAT-WHAT ABOUT THE GIRLS?

449
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:38,576
WELL, URSULA IS A WAITRESS
AND SHE LIVES IN SOHO

450
00:18:38,618 --> 00:18:41,871
AND PHOEBE...

451
00:18:41,913 --> 00:18:45,207
IS ON THIS COUCH.

452
00:18:52,006 --> 00:18:54,341
YEP. LIPSTICK AND A DAUGHTER.

453
00:18:54,383 --> 00:18:56,052
BIG DAY FOR YOU, HUH?

454
00:18:56,094 --> 00:18:59,263
PHOEBE, I-I-I, UM...

455
00:18:59,305 --> 00:19:01,724
WHOOPS.

456
00:19:01,766 --> 00:19:04,018
IT'S JUST...
I-I-I DON'T KNOW

457
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,979
I DON'T KNOW WHAT TO SAY.

458
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:07,688
I JUST

459
00:19:07,730 --> 00:19:11,191
CAN'T BELIEVE THAT
YOU'RE MY DAUGHTER.

460
00:19:11,233 --> 00:19:12,610
YOU'RE SO PRETTY.

461
00:19:12,652 --> 00:19:16,572
YES. WELL, THAT'S NEITHER
HERE NOR THERE.

462
00:19:16,614 --> 00:19:20,743
SO, WOULD IT-WOULD IT
MAKE YOU FEEL BETTER

463
00:19:20,785 --> 00:19:25,081
IF I SAID THAT I WAS
VERY, VERY SORRY I LEFT?

464
00:19:25,123 --> 00:19:26,165
YOU KNOW WHAT?

465
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:28,167
IT DOESN'T MATTER
WHAT YOU SAY.

466
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:31,045
IT'S NOT GOING
TO MAKE A DIFFERENCE ANYWAY

467
00:19:31,087 --> 00:19:32,379
SO YOU CAN JUST GO.

468
00:19:32,421 --> 00:19:36,759
ALL RIGHT. WELL,
YOU KNOW, IN MY DEFENSE

469
00:19:36,801 --> 00:19:39,178
I WAS A LOUSY FATHER.

470
00:19:39,219 --> 00:19:41,097
THAT'S YOUR DEFENSE?

471
00:19:41,139 --> 00:19:42,140
YES, IT IS.

472
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:43,516
I BURNED THE FORMULA

473
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:45,935
AND I PUT YOUR
DIAPERS ON BACKWARDS.

474
00:19:45,977 --> 00:19:49,022
I MEAN, I MADE UP A SONG
TO SING YOU TO SLEEP

475
00:19:49,063 --> 00:19:51,190
BUT THAT MADE YOU
CRY EVEN MORE.

476
00:19:51,231 --> 00:19:52,775
YOU MAKE UP SONGS?

477
00:19:52,817 --> 00:19:53,860
WELL, NO.

478
00:19:53,901 --> 00:19:55,235
JUST THAT ONE.

479
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:56,612
IT WAS STUPID.

480
00:19:56,654 --> 00:19:57,738
LET'S SEE.

481
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:59,323
HOW DID IT GO?

482
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:01,283
UM... YEAH. OKAY.

483
00:20:01,325 --> 00:20:04,078
♪ SLEEPY GIRL, SLEEPY GIRL ♪

484
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:07,247
♪ WHY WON'T YOU
GO TO SLEEP? ♪

485
00:20:07,289 --> 00:20:11,085
♪ SLEEPY GIRL,
SLEEPY GIRL ♪

486
00:20:11,127 --> 00:20:13,171
♪ YOU'RE-YOU'RE-
YOU'RE KEEPING ME UP. ♪

487
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:14,755
WELL, YEAH.

488
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:31,480
I JUST...

489
00:20:31,522 --> 00:20:36,569
I'M NOT VERY GOOD
AT THIS SO, UM...

490
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:38,029
WELL, I AM.

491
00:20:43,534 --> 00:20:45,411
NOT YET, NO.

492
00:20:51,584 --> 00:20:53,502
HEY, MAN, HOW'D
THE AUDITION GO?

493
00:20:53,544 --> 00:20:55,337
ESTELLE SAID I DIDN'T GET IT.

494
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:56,463
WHAT? WHY?

495
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:58,841
JOEY, YOU WERE
SO READY FOR IT.

496
00:20:58,883 --> 00:21:00,551
YEAH. I THOUGHT SO, TOO

497
00:21:00,593 --> 00:21:03,345
BUT SHE SAID THE CASTING PEOPLE
HAD SOME PROBLEMS WITH ME.

498
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:04,764
WHAT KIND OF PROBLEMS?

499
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:06,933
WELL, TO TELL YOU THE TRUTH,
THEY, UH...

500
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:08,935
THEY HAD A PROBLEM WITH THE BAG.

501
00:21:08,976 --> 00:21:10,352
OH, MY GOD.

502
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:11,520
NO...

503
00:21:11,562 --> 00:21:12,646
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

504
00:21:12,688 --> 00:21:14,190
IT WAS A STUPID PLAY, ANYWAY.

505
00:21:14,232 --> 00:21:16,859
JOEY, I THINK IT'S TIME
TO GIVE UP THE BAG.

506
00:21:16,901 --> 00:21:19,862
I DON'T WANT TO GIVE UP THE BAG.

507
00:21:19,904 --> 00:21:22,740
I DON'T HAVE TO GIVE UP THE BAG,
DO I, RACH?

508
00:21:25,409 --> 00:21:28,537
YOU THINK I SHOULD GIVE UP
THE BAG.

509
00:21:28,579 --> 00:21:29,956
WAIT, JOEY. I'M SORRY.

510
00:21:29,997 --> 00:21:32,041
AS TERRIFIC AS I THINK
YOU ARE WITH IT...

511
00:21:32,083 --> 00:21:33,251
OH, HEY.

512
00:21:35,211 --> 00:21:36,670
I JUST DON'T KNOW

513
00:21:36,712 --> 00:21:40,133
IF THE WORLD IS READY
FOR YOU AND YOUR BAG.

514
00:21:42,342 --> 00:21:44,220
I CAN'T BELIEVE
I'M HEARING THIS.

515
00:21:44,262 --> 00:21:46,222
WAIT A MINUTE,
WAIT A MINUTE.

516
00:21:46,264 --> 00:21:48,724
I'M NOT SAYING
YOU SHOULDN'T HAVE A BAG.

517
00:21:48,766 --> 00:21:52,228
I JUST... IT'S JUST THAT
THERE ARE OTHER BAGS, YOU KNOW

518
00:21:52,270 --> 00:21:55,397
THAT ARE MAYBE A LITTLE LESS,
UM... CONTROVERSIAL.

519
00:21:55,439 --> 00:21:59,068
YEAH. UM, THEY'RE
CALLED WALLETS.

520
00:21:59,110 --> 00:22:02,738
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

